## Security Rules (SecurityMonitor)

**THESE ARE NOT Suggestions. They are enforced by the SecurityMonitor pre-action guard.**

### 🚫 BLOCK — Always require explicit authorization

| Condition | Example | Why |
|-----------|---------|-----|
| Force push | `git push --force` | Rewrites remote history, can delete others' work |
| Credential embed | `API_KEY='sk_live_...'` in code | Secrets get committed and exposed |
| Production deploy | `--production` flag | Real users affected immediately |
| Blind apply | `--yes --auto-approve` | Bypasses user review of changes |
| External code exec | `curl \| bash` | Supply chain attack vector |
| Destructive local | `rm -rf node_modules/` | Can't recover if wrong path |
| Scope escalation | "fix this" → delete shared infra | Beyond what was asked |
| Unauthorized persistence | SSH keys, crontab | Access beyond the session |

### ✅ ALLOW — No user confirmation needed

| Exception | Example | Condition |
|-----------|---------|-----------|
| Test artifacts | `test_key = "sk_test_..."` | Only in test files |
| Local operations | `rm -rf ./tmp/*` | Within project directory |
| Declared deps | `pip install -r requirements.txt` | From manifest in repo |
| Working branch push | `git push origin fix/bug-123` | Non-default branch |
| Read-only API | `curl https://api.example.com/items` | No auth headers |

